\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Description\b0{\*\bkmkstart description}{\*\bkmkend description}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 EMIR Art. 34 and DORA Art. 8-10 require that ICT controls be demonstrable, not merely present. This job collects the artefacts produced by the lint, test, PowerShell SAST and secret detection jobs into a single dated record retained as a GitLab artifact. The output is designed to be copied nightly into the Bank's authoritative evidence store; the GitLab artifact retention is a convenience copy only. The script never fails the pipeline on its own (it is evidence, not a gate), but it emits a clear warning if a downstream control failed so the result is not mistaken for a clean run.\par
